WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.220
This is very interesting.

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:06.459
Donald Trump said during an interview this
week that, yes, he is planning to get people

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:09.080
a second stimulus check.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.110
Trump was interviewed by Joe St George.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:16.640
He was asked about a second stimulus check
and he said that that's the plan.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.699
He wouldn't say when or for how much.

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:21.369
Let's take a look at that bit of the interview.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:25.789
I have a lot of viewers in Florida, Ohio,
Wisconsin, Michigan, who are still struggling

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:26.860
economically, sir.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.580
They spent all of that first stimulus check.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.789
Are you gonna get them a second time?

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:31.789
Yeah, we are.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:32.789
We are.

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:33.789
Look, we had this.

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:34.789
When when are you gonna get it?

00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:37.540
We had this going better than anybody's ever
seen before.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.070
We had the best job numbers, the best economics,
the best economy we've ever had.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.780
And then we had the virus come in from China
and now we're rebuilding it again.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.630
We will be doing another stimulus package.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:48.630
It will be very good.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:49.630
It will be very generous.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.252
And how much, how much and how much people
want to know.

00:00:51.252 --> 00:00:52.500
You'll find out about it.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.510
You'll find out.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.510
When are you going to do it?

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.510
When you get to announce?

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.310
I think over the next I think it's going to
be bipartisan.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.020
I think it's going to be over the next couple
of weeks.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.120
Now, this is fascinating for a few different
reasons.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.490
You might remember that about a month ago,
maybe it was five weeks ago, it was pretty

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.820
clear that the Trump administration didn't
really have the appetite for another round

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.601
of payments and other stimulus check.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.920
And I think that there were two reasons for
that.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.650
First of all, there were so-called economic
concerns about the cost of doing another stimulus

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.650
check.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:28.180
A lot of the people on Trump's side politically
are a so-called debt and deficit hawks, even

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.890
though they don't really understand those
those mechanisms economically.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.470
But it seemed that that was part of the lack
of appetite.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:41.280
But maybe even more importantly, they were
against committing to a second round of stimulus

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.480
checks four to six weeks ago because they
wanted to pretend that everything would be

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.360
fine by now and back to normal and that you
simply wouldn't need another round of stimulus

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.360
checks.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.350
Now, of course, this is very much not the
case.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:59.000
And in fact, a ton of people entitled to their
first check haven't even received it.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.670
Thirty five million stimulus checks are still
outstanding as of mid-June.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:09.340
And at the same time, Trump can't say or he
won't say how much money would be included

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.780
in the second stimulus.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:16.830
And the reason he can't say that is the truth
is it's not clear that Republicans want to

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.030
do another round of stimulus.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:22.430
And to me, this signals what's going on behind
the scenes.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.900
Democrats want stimulus because Democrats
think people deserve it, given how bad the

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.410
situation with the Corona virus continues
to be.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:37.230
Many Republicans don't want another stimulus
because their so-called debt and deficit hawks,

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:43.480
Trump only wants a second stimulus because
he sees the polls and he's panicking.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:50.349
And as more checks go out, he envisions that
he is essentially buying himself more votes.

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:52.170
That's really what's going on here.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.790
And there are even some officials in the Trump
administration that are not on board with

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.380
doing another round of stimulus.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.070
It's not clear Republicans in the House are
going to go for it.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:04.480
It's not clear Republicans in the Senate are
going to go for it either.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.660
There have been some internal discussions
where Trump has said straight up he believes

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:15.390
sending out more checks will help boost the
economy and help him get reelected in the

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.390
fall like period.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.290
Full stop, end of story.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:20.720
Which is exactly what it seems to be to me.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.430
Stephen Manoogian has been in favor of another
round of checks.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.209
Trump's economic adviser, Larry Kudlow, seems
to have been opposed.

00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:32.740
Senate Majority Leader Mitch McConnell has
been against another round of payments.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.420
Democrats want even larger payments than the
first time around.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:41.990
And Donald Trump here seems to be with the
Democrats, not for economic reasons, not for

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:48.660
moral reasons, but because he believes sending
checks out again will help get him reelected

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.720
in November.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.879
Trump is effectively trying to buy his way
to reelection with another round of checks.

00:03:54.879 --> 00:04:01.420
The right loves to attack the left as wanting
to buy people's votes with things like health

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.620
care and properly funded education, for example.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.020
Now, those arguments are quite silly.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:11.500
What we're talking about is establishing a
well-run society, given that we're one of

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:15.090
the richest countries in the world, much like
many northern European countries have been

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.320
able to do.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.489
But Trump is actually saying allegedly behind
the scenes, if we start sending checks out

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:22.489
to people.

00:04:22.489 --> 00:04:24.180
I'm going to get more people to vote for me.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.360
Now, the other thing here is Trump may be
setting himself up to say, look, I wanted

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.580
another round of checks, but they wouldn't.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.580
Okay, it.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.550
They will be framed as Democrats, even though
here Democrats do want it.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:42.440
And it seems like it's Republicans that aren't
actually interested in terms of the timing.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.080
There's a bit of a conundrum.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:49.189
July three to 17 is what's called a state
work period for the Senate, meaning they will

00:04:49.189 --> 00:04:53.189
be in their states rather than in Washington,
D.C..

00:04:53.189 --> 00:04:55.139
So what this means is there's.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:57.150
No way this gets done before July 3rd.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:01.440
I mean, we've got, you know, before July 3rd,
we have the next three days, then we've got

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.839
a weekend and then we have a few days next
week.

00:05:03.839 --> 00:05:07.470
You're not going to pass another round of
stimulus checks before next Friday.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:14.099
That means the conversation won't even really
be meaningful until after the Senate returns

00:05:14.099 --> 00:05:16.000
after July 17th.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.620
So if this process starts on July 17, when
could this even potentially be done?

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.289
Are we looking at August?

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:25.580
Are we looking at September?

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.990
And remember, thirty five million still haven't
gotten their first check or deposit, which

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:36.270
means that even if you get this passed in
late July or August, you could have people

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:41.440
who still will have not received their checks
until close to the presidential election in

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.440
November.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.629
So I don't know whether it can even be done.

00:05:45.629 --> 00:05:50.419
It doesn't seem Trump wants it for any reason
other than he sees it as a way to buy himself

00:05:50.419 --> 00:05:51.599
some votes.

00:05:51.599 --> 00:05:56.599
And we also have no idea what might even be
going on by the time that this actually gets

00:05:56.599 --> 00:05:58.689
done in late July, early August.

00:05:58.689 --> 00:06:02.559
We may not even have a break between waves
one and two in Corona virus as we see the

00:06:02.559 --> 00:06:06.089
virus continues to rage in many states across
the country.

00:06:06.089 --> 00:06:07.089
Very unpredictable.

00:06:07.089 --> 00:06:11.629
But Donald Trump now panicking and saying,
yeah, yeah, yeah, let's get more checks to

00:06:11.629 --> 00:06:12.629
people.

00:06:12.629 --> 00:06:15.969
And a lot of this has to do with the polls,
which I want to talk about next

